{
  "case_id": "2009-08-604",
  "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 12:59 p.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Union Pacific Railroad",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 3 First (q) of the Railway Labor Act says that the findings in an order of the division shall be conclusive on the parties, except that the order of the division may be set aside for one of three specified reasons. As a matter of plain dictionary meaning in this context, \"except\" means that there are three and only three exceptions to the otherwise conclusive nature of these awards."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why isn't its judgment that there's a statutory violation what's at issue before us, because that's what they said?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Union Pacific Railroad",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, on -- on page 5 of their brief to the Seventh Circuit, they waived any argument based on that first statutory ground of review. There was a first count in their petition for review that was based on that statutory ground, and on page 5 they renounced it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you -- do you dispute what your opponent tells us, that some panels of the board, even when there has been no conference, let alone no proof of a conference, but some panels have stayed proceedings to allow the conference to occur, and then the board will pick up?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Union Pacific Railroad",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that there are several things wrong with it, Your Honor, starting from the premise that the statute guarantees in all instances procedures that are, quote unquote, \"fair\" in an untethered sense. This statute guarantees specific procedural rights, which if you put them together do guarantee fair procedures. But it doesn't guarantee fairness in the abstract."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Then if -- then a person following this is obliged not to pay heed to this advice because if you don't put in every document, if you don't put in enough evidence of conferencing, you are going to be out and never have your grievance heard."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ballenger",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, the board obviously does not consider evidence of conferencing unnecessary, Your Honor. It has held for a very long time, going back, I think, 40 years to Award 18679 at least, that evidence of conferencing is essential to the board's consideration of any dispute under the terms of the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Thomas H. Geoghegan",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The conferencing, by the way, is in Section 2 of the Railway Labor Act. The board and its power and procedures is in Section 3. Section 3 has no mention of conferencing whatsoever in it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: I -- I still don't understand your answer to the Chief Justice's question about how the panels -- how these panels -- how the board, in your view, is supposed to go about making some sort of sensible procedural rules about establishing the that conferencing took place."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. GEOGHEGAN",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We don't think that the board can or should do that. What we do think is that, if there is -- the rule that I just read from, 301.5, says that you raise relevant argumentative facts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I thought your position was -- at least I thought I heard you say earlier, that these individual panels do not have rulemaking authority for the board. I'm looking at something that says, \"National Railway Adjustment Board, Uniform Rules of Procedure, Revised June 23rd.\" That's put out by the -- the board, the one that you said that is --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. GEOGHEGAN",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think of it as relevant, probative evidence as to conferencing when the objection had not been raised at the time that these cases were conferenced, at the time that this --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. BALLENGER",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Four quick points. Justice Stevens, the awards that you are"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Were any of those decisions that were boardwise or did they apply to one panel?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: But there is a difference between governmentally ordered arbitrations and private contracts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Respondent suggests that the Steelworker trilogy standard that this Court has articulated for labor arbitration generally doesn't apply under the RLA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, Respondent focuses a lot on section 301.5 in its language about argumentative facts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ballenger",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The relevant standard is if the board is even arguably construing or applying the relevant rules and its decision stands, even if a court is convinced that the arbitrator committed serious error."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-604",
      "confidence": 0.0,
